{"content":"Perfect! Now I have all the details I need to answer the question. Let me compile the answer:\n\nq20.\n\n**Mechanism**: Server-Sent Events (SSE)\n\n**Hub path**: `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go`\n\n**Handler names that broadcast through the hub**:\n1. `CreateMemo`\n2. `CreateMemoComment`\n3. `UpdateMemo` (via `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects`)\n4. `DeleteMemo`\n5. `UpsertMemoReaction`\n6. `DeleteMemoReaction`\n\n**Details**:\n\nThe server uses **Server-Sent Events (SSE)** to push live events to browsers via the `/api/v1/sse` endpoint (server/router/api/v1/sse_handler.go:25). Clients subscribe with authentication and maintain a persistent HTTP connection.\n\nThe **SSEHub** (server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go:56) manages client connections and broadcasts events. It uses a map to track connected clients, with each client receiving events through a buffered channel (32-event buffer). The `Broadcast` method sends events to all connected clients with visibility-based filtering (Private events only go to the creator or admins; Public/Protected events go to all).\n\nThe **six memo handlers** that broadcast events are:\n- **CreateMemo** (server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:70) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoCreated`\n- **CreateMemoComment** (server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:20) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoCommentCreated`\n- **UpdateMemo** (server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:401) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoUpdated` via `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects`\n- **DeleteMemo** (server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:518) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoDeleted`\n- **UpsertMemoReaction** (server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go:60) — broadcasts `SSEEventReactionUpserted`\n- **DeleteMemoReaction** (server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go:111) — broadcasts `SSEEventReactionDeleted`","iteration":11,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
